#! category: furniture
#! great cistern - a tin-lined belly sunk to its rim in the earth
#! Sunk to the rim, so there is no vessel to draw - only the mouth and the ring
#! of stone holding it. The first attempt filled the mouth with solid body and
#! read as a boulder; the water is stippled now, which gives it a surface instead
#! of a mass. Two short highlight dashes are the light on it, and the bright inner
#! ring is what makes the mouth read as an opening rather than a lid.
